UTILITY: wget (BusyBox 1.38)
ADMITTED: -q, -S, -T SEC, -O FILE, -U AGENT, --no-check-certificate
BANNED: --tries, --timeout, -c, --post-data, --post-file
EXIT_STATUS: 0 success, 1 any failure (DNS, 404, timeout, bad option)
SEMANTICS: -T covers connect and read, not DNS; wrap the call in
  sh/lib/timeout.sh for an overall wall-clock bound. -q -S sends headers to
  stderr; never parse them.
RATIONALE: sole sanctioned HTTPS edge; not part of the POSIX core
